## Context and authority

Filed from replicator 0003 (branch `t0003-gavard`, commit `03af9ef`) at the
author's request, 2026-11-27. Separate from 1572 because a harness session is
working on 1572/1573/1574; this ticket touches none of them. One opus
executor ran `/replicate` assess and reproduce on Gavard and Schoch (2026),
transcribing the authors' Stata package to Python, then compared it with the
author's September 2026 Python port. Evidence in replicator:
`replications/gavard2026climate/` (README.md, reproduce/README.md section
"Stata semantics", COMPARE-PORT.md) and
`memory/journal/2026/2026-11-27-gavard-stata-transcription.md`.
Result: 1,032/1,032 printed table values and 104/104 A1 values match; 177
disagreements with the port, all in four unprinted `gmm` models (a
translation error, an added constant). One paper: the observations below
are evidence, not established Stata behaviour, unless marked documented.

## Request A: a Stata-caveats reference

The author asked to keep what decided the matches. Proposed home:
`references/stata-caveats.md`, pointed to from `reproduce` when the package
is Stata and no licence is available. Generic rules only; paper cases stay
in replicator.

- Documented (to cite from the manual): `generate`/`egen` create float (float32) by default and
  `replace` keeps the type. Reproduce storage types; all-double computation
  moved six printed values across a rounding boundary in this case.
- Documented (to cite from the manual): an expression without a `by` prefix indexes rows of the whole
  dataset (`x[17]`); division by zero gives missing.
- To verify against the `gmm` manual (the executor's recollection, not checked): `{xb: varlist}` adds no constant and `instruments()` adds one. The specification difference explained all 177 disagreements.
- Observed, check per case: `xtgee` working correlation from pooled
  residual-moment sums divided by pooled pair counts, then by SSR/N; robust
  VCE times (N-1)/(N-P) for `rgf` and G/(G-1) for panel clustering.
- Open: the default second-step weight of `gmm ... vce(cluster)`.
- Method: when an implicit convention is fixed by matching printed tables,
  name the tables used for the choice and score the held-out tables
  separately (here Tables 1 and B3 used, seven tables held out).

## Request B: skill findings from the run

| # | Finding | Overlap |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `references/gavard-scotch-mapping.md` carries the port's findings, so it is an answer key for any validation on this paper | new |
| 2 | `fetch.sh`/manifest assume a downloadable package; a privately e-mailed package has no path (`source_url: null` used) | new |
| 3 | Translated reproduction is described only under selected-claim confirmation; nothing says whether a translated run supports `cra_reussie` | new |
| 4 | Fixing implicit estimator conventions by matching published tables needs a used/held-out split (Request A, method item) | new |
| 5 | `out/*.csv` has no place for estimates the paper does not print (executor added `reproduce-unprinted.csv`, `extras.csv`) | new |
| 6 | Half-unit rule undefined for printed ranges ("0.05-0.12") and bounds ("more than 0.24") | new |
| 7 | Three-digit precision undefined when comparing two reproductions (half-unit vs equal rounded strings) | near 1572 finding 7, distinct case |
| 8 | assess step 5 needs a Zotero publication an unattended run cannot do | new |

Replicator-owned, not requested here: the folder-layout ticket's first-use
update of replicator AGENTS.md/README.md.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Receiving Imagine records facts, overlap with 1572-1574, ownership and
  standing rulings, and disposes of Request A and each finding in Request B.
- [ ] If accepted, the Stata reference states for each item whether it is
  documented Stata behaviour or a one-case observation.

## Receiving Imagine — 2026-11-27

Facts against framing: read the pinned Replicator 03af9ef source, including
COMPARE-PORT.md and the transcription journal, against current skill contracts.
The matches are case observations; the historical Stata release, update, and
settings remain unknown. Official Release 19 manuals correct the proposed
blanket replace-keeps-type claim (promotion is documented), qualify numeric
generate defaults with set type, and distinguish documented GMM constants and
weight options from the unverified historical behavior. No scientific estimates
were rerun. Primary evidence and page references are in the receiving handoff.

Overlap: 1573 and 1574 are merged (data auditing and asserted robustness checks).
1572 retains translation/scoring decisions. Existing selected-claim freezes and
probe validation boundaries supply reusable contracts; they do not yet cover
all validation exposure, private package intake, or auxiliary unprinted outputs.
The current Zotero section already keeps drafts pending review and merge;
B8 needs no new publishing authority or implementation.

Ownership: the harness owns generic skill contracts and references. Replicator
owns paper cases, scientific outputs, and its benchmark cohort. No edits to its
source tree are accepted here. A generic reference cannot decide historical
software semantics from table matches or authorize translation by itself.

Standing rulings: preserve canonical ACRe and whole-paper/selected-target
meanings, printed-digit tolerance, signed probe execution, and outward gates.
A join audit supplies evidence, never an additional Fully gate. No subjective
probabilities, paid API calls, new estimates, or signing authority are introduced.

| Request | Disposition and rationale |
|---|---|
| A | Accept corrected/version-qualified manual evidence in 1576, after 1577. Separate documentation, inference, case calibration, and historical uncertainty; no case-fit formula becomes a default. |
| B1/B4 | Accept 1577. Read worked examples only after checking validation exposure. Same-paper unused tables differ from fresh-paper validation. Freeze calibration choices and preserve post-hoc disclosures. |
| B2 | Accept 1578. Support caller-supplied private bytes, source_url null, provenance, and representation-specific hashes without implying redistribution or author contact. |
| B3 | Hold for author: whether translated execution establishes canonical CRA is a methodology decision. No child resolves it. |
| B5 | Accept 1579. Retain produced unprinted estimates in an auxiliary artifact outside scored comparisons; do not invent a published comparator. |
| B6/B7 | Hold for author: printed bounds/ranges and cross-port precision conventions require a scoring decision. Preserve existing rules. |
| B8 | Already covered: assess drafts locally; publication follows the host review/merge gate and can remain pending. |

The accepted children preserve the source intent with narrower documented
scope. Parent 1575 tracks delivery and the held questions; merging reception
neither closes it nor grants implementation priority beyond the author's
explicit raid-on-acceptance instruction. Prior blind-spot review was CLEAN;
fresh same-family read-only pass found one material omission: private local
bytes must also compose with blind assessment. Added to 1578. Auxiliary CSV
exclusions must reach broad output/schema/count guidance in 1579. No other
material omissions. Requested seat Sol 6.1 medium, actual identity unobserved;
no independent-review claim.
